{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The strongest RNA-only models use scvi_n200 with multiprofile and avgpool/transformer, reaching about 0.65 accuracy and 0.63 F1, while the only tested multimodal model (config_030: scvi_n200, multiprofile, ResNet, avgpool, concat) is slightly lower at 0.6315 accuracy and 0.6068 F1. Image-only ResNet is also weak, so it is unclear whether concat fusion is the bottleneck or whether the image branch is simply not helpful. config_031 changes only fusion to weighted while keeping the exact same RNA encoder, image encoder, profile setting, and aggregation as config_030, so it cleanly isolates the effect of fusion. This is the best next experiment because it is a minimal one-factor extension of the most informative multimodal result, directly tests whether adaptive fusion can make multimodal modeling competitive with the strong RNA-only baseline, and avoids changing multiple design choices at once."
}

